## 3. Database Schema (PostgreSQL via Prisma)

### 3A. Users Table
```sql
Table: users
- id              UUID PRIMARY KEY
- phone           VARCHAR(15) UNIQUE NOT NULL   -- Primary login method
- email           VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE           -- Optional
- name            VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
- role            ENUM('customer','owner','driver','admin') DEFAULT 'customer'
- is_verified     BOOLEAN DEFAULT false         -- Phone OTP verified
- created_at      TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
- updated_at      TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
```

### 3B. Businesses Table (Owner/Agency)
```sql
Table: businesses
- id              UUID PRIMARY KEY
- user_id         UUID REFERENCES users(id)     -- The owner's user account
- business_name   VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
- type            ENUM('individual','agency')
- operating_zone  VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL         -- Primary pickup area
- nid_front_url   TEXT                          -- Cloudinary URL
- nid_back_url    TEXT
- trade_license_url TEXT                        -- NULL for individuals
- address_proof_url TEXT
- bkash_number    VARCHAR(15)
- nagad_number    VARCHAR(15)
- bank_account    TEXT                          -- Optional JSON {bank, branch, acc_no}
- status          ENUM('pending','approved','rejected','suspended') DEFAULT 'pending'
- rejection_reason TEXT                         -- Filled on rejection
- approved_at     TIMESTAMP
- created_at      TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
```

### 3C. Cars Table (Many cars per business)
```sql
Table: cars
- id                    UUID PRIMARY KEY
- business_id           UUID REFERENCES businesses(id)   -- ONE business → MANY cars
- model                 VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL            -- e.g. "Toyota Axio"
- manufacturing_year    INT                              -- Optional
- seat_count            INT NOT NULL                     -- 4, 6, 7, 11, etc.
- car_type              ENUM('sedan','suv','microbus','noah_hiace','other')
- color                 VARCHAR(50)
- number_plate          VARCHAR(20) UNIQUE NOT NULL
- photo_front_url       TEXT
- photo_back_url        TEXT
- photo_inside_url      TEXT
- brta_doc_url          TEXT
- fitness_cert_url      TEXT
- fitness_expiry_date   DATE NOT NULL                    -- Required; auto-suspend logic uses this
- tax_token_url         TEXT
- tax_token_expiry_date DATE
- insurance_url         TEXT                             -- Optional
- status                ENUM('pending','approved','rejected','active','inactive','suspended') DEFAULT 'pending'
- rejection_reason      TEXT
- is_available          BOOLEAN DEFAULT true             -- Owner toggle
- created_at            TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
```

### 3D. Drivers Table
```sql
Table: drivers
- id                UUID PRIMARY KEY
- business_id       UUID REFERENCES businesses(id)
- car_id            UUID REFERENCES cars(id)             -- Currently assigned car
- name              VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
- phone             VARCHAR(15) NOT NULL
- license_front_url TEXT
- license_back_url  TEXT
- photo_url         TEXT
- experience_years  INT                                  -- Optional
- status            ENUM('pending','approved','suspended','blocked') DEFAULT 'pending'
- created_at        TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
```

### 3E. Bookings Table (Core of the platform)
```sql
Table: bookings
- id                UUID PRIMARY KEY
- customer_id       UUID REFERENCES users(id)
- car_id            UUID REFERENCES cars(id)             -- Assigned after matching
- driver_id         UUID REFERENCES drivers(id)          -- Assigned by admin
- service_type      ENUM('car_rental','airport_transfer','intercity','travel_tour','event_wedding','corporate')
- status            ENUM('pending','confirmed','ongoing','completed','cancelled') DEFAULT 'pending'

-- Common fields (always present)
- customer_name     VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
- customer_phone    VARCHAR(15) NOT NULL
- pickup_area       VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL                -- Structured area, NOT free text
- pickup_date       DATE NOT NULL
- pickup_time       TIME NOT NULL
- car_type_pref     ENUM('sedan','suv','microbus','noah_hiace','any') DEFAULT 'any'
- passenger_count   INT DEFAULT 1
- special_note      TEXT

-- Service-specific fields (stored as JSONB for flexibility)
- service_data      JSONB NOT NULL                       -- All extra fields per service (see Phase 2)

-- Payment
- estimated_fare    DECIMAL(10,2)
- advance_amount    DECIMAL(10,2)                        -- 20% of estimated_fare
- advance_paid      BOOLEAN DEFAULT false
- advance_payment_method ENUM('bkash','bank','sslcommerz')
- advance_txn_id    VARCHAR(255)

-- Trip lifecycle
- trip_started_at   TIMESTAMP
- trip_ended_at     TIMESTAMP

-- Final payment
- final_amount      DECIMAL(10,2)                        -- Entered after trip
- amount_received   DECIMAL(10,2)
- commission_amount DECIMAL(10,2)                        -- Auto-calculated 10%
- payment_status    ENUM('unpaid','partial','paid') DEFAULT 'unpaid'
- payment_method    ENUM('cash','bkash','nagad','bank')

-- Meta
- created_at        TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
- updated_at        TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
```

### 3F. Reviews Table
```sql
Table: reviews
- id            UUID PRIMARY KEY
- booking_id    UUID REFERENCES bookings(id) UNIQUE
- customer_id   UUID REFERENCES users(id)
- car_id        UUID REFERENCES cars(id)
- driver_id     UUID REFERENCES drivers(id)
- rating        INT CHECK (rating >= 1 AND rating <= 5)
- comment       TEXT
- created_at    TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
```

### 3G. Subscriptions Table
```sql
Table: subscription_plans
- id            UUID PRIMARY KEY
- name          VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL          -- e.g. Free, Premium, Business
- price         DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL
- duration_days INT NOT NULL
- car_limit     INT                            -- Max cars allowed under this plan
- visibility_priority INT DEFAULT 0            -- Higher = shown first in listings
- commission_rate DECIMAL(5,2) DEFAULT 10.00  -- % commission
- features      JSONB                          -- Array of feature strings
- is_active     BOOLEAN DEFAULT true

Table: business_subscriptions
- id            UUID PRIMARY KEY
- business_id   UUID REFERENCES businesses(id)
- plan_id       UUID REFERENCES subscription_plans(id)
- starts_at     TIMESTAMP NOT NULL
- expires_at    TIMESTAMP NOT NULL
- status        ENUM('active','expired','cancelled')
```

### 3H. Notifications Table
```sql
Table: notifications
- id            UUID PRIMARY KEY
- user_id       UUID REFERENCES users(id)
- type          VARCHAR(100)                   -- e.g. 'booking_confirmed', 'doc_approved'
- title         VARCHAR(255)
- body          TEXT
- is_read       BOOLEAN DEFAULT false
- created_at    TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
```

---

## 4. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

| Route Pattern | Allowed Roles |
|---|---|
| `/` (homepage), `/book/*` | Public (all) |
| `/customer/*` | `customer` only |
| `/owner/*` | `owner` only, and `status = approved` |
| `/admin/*` | `admin` only |
| `GET /api/cars/search` | Public — BUT query MUST include `WHERE cars.status = 'active' AND businesses.status = 'approved'` |

**Middleware Logic (`rbac.js`):**
1. Extract JWT from Authorization header
2. Decode and get `role` and `id`
3. Match against route pattern
4. If mismatch → return `403 Forbidden`
5. Never trust client-side role — always re-validate from DB on sensitive operations

---

## 5. API Endpoint Structure (REST)

### Auth
```
POST   /api/auth/send-otp          ← Send OTP to phone number
POST   /api/auth/verify-otp        ← Verify OTP, return JWT
POST   /api/auth/login             ← Email/password fallback
POST   /api/auth/logout
```

### Bookings
```
POST   /api/bookings               ← Create a new booking
GET    /api/bookings               ← List (filtered by role: customer sees own, admin sees all)
GET    /api/bookings/:id           ← Booking detail
PATCH  /api/bookings/:id/status    ← Update status (role-restricted)
PATCH  /api/bookings/:id/start-trip
PATCH  /api/bookings/:id/end-trip
PATCH  /api/bookings/:id/payment   ← Record final payment
```

### Cars & Matching
```
GET    /api/cars/search?area=X&service=Y&passengers=N   ← Customer search
GET    /api/cars/match?passengers=N                     ← Seat matching algorithm
POST   /api/cars                   ← Owner adds a car
PATCH  /api/cars/:id               ← Owner updates car info
PATCH  /api/cars/:id/availability  ← Toggle available/unavailable
```

### Owner/Business
```
POST   /api/owners/register        ← Submit full registration (Steps 1–6)
GET    /api/owners/me              ← Owner's own dashboard data
GET    /api/owners/:id/bookings    ← Bookings for this owner's cars
PATCH  /api/owners/:id/documents   ← Update a specific document
```

### Admin
```
GET    /api/admin/dashboard        ← KPI stats
GET    /api/admin/registrations    ← Queue of pending businesses
PATCH  /api/admin/businesses/:id/approve
PATCH  /api/admin/businesses/:id/reject
PATCH  /api/admin/cars/:id/approve
PATCH  /api/admin/cars/:id/reject
GET    /api/admin/bookings         ← All bookings
PATCH  /api/admin/bookings/:id/assign   ← Assign driver/car
GET    /api/admin/payments
GET    /api/admin/subscriptions
```

---

## 6. Automated Jobs (Cron)

| Job | Schedule | Action |
|---|---|---|
| Fitness certificate expiry check | Daily at midnight | Set `cars.status = 'suspended'` where `fitness_expiry_date < TODAY` |
| Tax token expiry check | Daily at midnight | Same logic for tax token |
| Subscription expiry check | Daily at midnight | Set `business_subscriptions.status = 'expired'`, downgrade visibility |
| Renewal reminder SMS | 7 days before expiry | Send SMS to business owner |

---

## 7. Security Requirements

- All file upload endpoints: validate MIME type (accept only `image/jpeg`, `image/png`, `application/pdf`)
- Max file size: 5MB per document
- Uploaded files renamed to UUID before storage (prevent enumeration attacks)
- All admin endpoints require `role = 'admin'` in JWT AND in DB (double check)
- Rate limit OTP endpoint: max 3 OTP requests per phone per hour
